; PLEASE KEEP THE MINGW/COREDLL*.DEF AND W32API/LIBCE/COREDLL*.DEF
; FILES IN SYNC.
; COREDLL import surface for Windows Embedded CE 6.0 (i386-wince-mingw32ce)
; Base: Windows CE 6.0 shared source, private/winceos/coreos/core/dll/
; USR/coredll.def (-> core_common.def) + crt/corelib1.def.
; Parsing policy: x86 retail (ARM/PPC/MIPS/SH and DEBUG blocks excluded),
; every @CESYSGEN branch included (superset surface: individual devices
; export only what their OS image was built with).  NONAME (ordinal-only)
; exports are included with their ordinals (Name @n NONAME) so the import
; library binds by ordinal, exactly like the Microsoft SDK import
; libraries; a name-based lookup of those would fail at load time.
; Derived from the validated arm-wince-mingw32ce coredll6.def by applying
; exactly the arch-specific delta the shared source declares: the ARM-only
; exports removed, the x86-only exports added (see the grouped block near
; the end).  Cross-checked against the CE 6.0 X86 COREDLL def in the shared
; source (PUBLIC/COMMON/OAK/LIB/X86).
; Restored TlsAlloc/TlsFree per MSDN ("TlsAlloc"/"TlsFree", Link Library:
; Coredll.lib, "Windows CE 1.0 and later"): the device/SDK dump these defs were
; verified against omitted them (the same gap the CE 5.0 coredll.def records),
; but they are coremain coredll exports on every CE generation and clang's
; emulated TLS (__emutls_get_address) imports TlsAlloc/TlsFree, so a CE 6.0 program
; using thread_local would fail to link without them.
;
; ARM and x86 never share objects, so the two defs cannot be merged: x86
; coredll carries the SEH/EH runtime and the x86 compiler helpers in-DLL,
; while ARM forwards its floating point to FPCRT and spells the C++ EH/RTTI
; exports with __cdecl mangling (QAA/UAA/AAA) instead of MSVC/__thiscall
; (QAE/UAE/AAE).
; 2079 exports total (incl. 11 ordinal-only).

LIBRARY COREDLL
EXPORTS
; x86 (MSVC/__thiscall) spellings of the C++ EH/RTTI exports;
; ARM spells these QAA/UAA/AAA (__cdecl), x86 spells them
; QAE/UAE/AAE/QBE/UBE and the EH vector helpers YGX (stdcall).
??0exception@std@@QAE@ABV01@@Z
??0exception@std@@QAE@PBD@Z
??0exception@std@@QAE@XZ
??0type_info@@AAE@ABV0@@Z
??1exception@std@@UAE@XZ
??1type_info@@UAE@XZ
??4exception@std@@QAEAAV01@ABV01@@Z
??4type_info@@AAEAAV0@ABV0@@Z
??8type_info@@QBEHABV0@@Z
??9type_info@@QBEHABV0@@Z
??_L@YGXPAXIHP6EX0@Z1@Z
??_M@YGXPAXIHP6EX0@Z@Z
??_N@YGXPAXIHP6EX0@Z1@Z
??__C@YGXPAX0IHP6EX00@ZP6EX0@Z@Z
??__D@YGXPAX0IHP6EX00@ZP6EX0@Z@Z
?before@type_info@@QBEHABV1@@Z
?name@type_info@@QBEPBDXZ
?raw_name@type_info@@QBEPBDXZ
?what@exception@std@@UBEPBDXZ
??2@YAPAXI@Z
??2@YAPAXIABUnothrow_t@std@@@Z
??3@YAXPAX@Z
??3@YAXPAXABUnothrow_t@std@@@Z
??_7exception@std@@6B@
??_7type_info@@6B@
??_U@YAPAXI@Z
??_U@YAPAXIABUnothrow_t@std@@@Z
??_V@YAXPAX@Z
??_V@YAXPAXABUnothrow_t@std@@@Z
?__set_inconsistency@@YAP6AXXZP6AXXZ@Z
?_inconsistency@@YAXXZ
?_Nomemory@std@@YAXXZ
?_query_new_handler@@YAP6AHI@ZXZ
?_query_new_mode@@YAHXZ
?_set_new_handler@@YAP6AHI@ZP6AHI@Z@Z
?_set_new_mode@@YAHH@Z
?_Xlen@std@@YAXXZ
?_Xran@std@@YAXXZ
?nothrow@std@@3Unothrow_t@1@B
?set_new_handler@@YAP6AXXZP6AXXZ@Z
?set_terminate@std@@YAP6AXXZP6AXXZ@Z
?set_unexpected@std@@YAP6AXXZP6AXXZ@Z
?terminate@std@@YAXXZ
?uncaught_exception@std@@YA_NXZ
?unexpected@std@@YAXXZ
